This patch adds a new room type to the game, the "island."  It is a
room with at least one row of water lining the walls along the inside.
 It can appear from level three on, though on levels 3 and 4 it can
only appear in the same kinds of places as shops (to prevent the room
from blocking progress).  In case the player teleports or falls there
without a means of escape, there's also always a trap door somewhere
in the room.

There is no noise warning when this room is on your level (this may
change), and it is not guarenteed to be lit, so it's worth being
careful when entering.  Methods for crossing the water are left for
the player to determine, but there are several possibilities.  Note
that on deeper levels the room may have extra water, a single eel, or
contain lava instead of water.

Inside the moat, near the center, there is always a tree.  (Didn't you
know all desert islands have a palm tree on them?)  There is also a
spot on the ground marked with an 'X', for some mysterious purpose.

